to character and fact.

1362
01:18:54,960 --> 01:18:57,255
One who is accused with her
nonetheless.

1363
01:18:59,130 --> 01:19:00,910
Get on with it, Sir James.

1364
01:19:03,030 --> 01:19:05,780
My Lord, on the 11th of June last year,

1365
01:19:06,240 --> 01:19:11,220
Mrs Mills was before you
prosecuting two drug addicts for murder.

1366
01:19:12,010 --> 01:19:14,246
A case in which I myself was involved.

1367
01:19:14,480 --> 01:19:17,186
She was also before me
in an injunction hearing

1368
01:19:17,480 --> 01:19:20,219
about a minor
who didn˙t want a heart transplant.

1369
01:19:20,220 --> 01:19:22,419
It appears that had ended by the 11th.

1370
01:19:22,420 --> 01:19:24,380
Yes, well, the hearing had.

1371
01:19:24,720 --> 01:19:28,700
The boy died
immediately following the operation.

1372
01:19:29,330 --> 01:19:33,340
Mrs Mills was upset as a result,
was she not?

1373
01:19:34,800 --> 01:19:35,970
Extremely.

1374
01:19:38,470 --> 01:19:41,160
She called on you at your lodgings.

1375
01:19:42,870 --> 01:19:45,830
Can you tell the committee
what happened?

1376
01:19:46,310 --> 01:19:49,710
Yes, she appeared drunk,
she got more drunk,

1377
01:19:50,250 --> 01:19:52,090
finally she collapsed

1378
01:19:53,680 --> 01:19:55,430
and I put her to bed.

1379
01:19:55,750 --> 01:19:58,060
- At the lodgings?
- Yes.

1380
01:19:59,320 --> 01:20:02,130
- In whose bed did she sleep?
- Mine.

1381
01:20:04,630 --> 01:20:10,050
Sir John, would you mind telling
the committee where you slept?

1382
01:20:11,540 --> 01:20:13,470
I didn˙t, for the most part.

1383
01:20:15,610 --> 01:20:19,010
I was concerned that
she didn˙t vomit and choke.

1384
01:20:21,850 --> 01:20:25,510
Did you and Mrs Mills sleep together?

1385
01:20:30,650 --> 01:20:31,650
No.

1386
01:20:39,160 --> 01:20:42,513
VALENTINE: Are you absolutely
certain about that, My Lord?

1387
01:20:42,700 --> 01:20:44,429
I think I might have remembered.

1388
01:20:44,430 --> 01:20:48,120
- Do you remember?
- Yes. I˙ve given you my answer.

1389
01:20:48,740 --> 01:20:51,960
Then perhaps you can tell us
what you did that night?

1390
01:20:52,480 --> 01:20:55,060
I˙ve told you.
I made sure she didn˙t choke.

1391
01:20:57,080 --> 01:20:58,420
I see.

1392
01:20:58,680 --> 01:21:00,230
Sir John.

1393
01:21:00,520 --> 01:21:04,740
Did you have sex with this lady
while she was in your bed?

1394
01:21:05,390 --> 01:21:08,567
Whilst she was drunk?
That would be very ungentlemanly.

1395
01:21:09,090 --> 01:21:10,550
Don˙t you think?

1396
01:21:13,530 --> 01:21:16,490
Regrettably, I haven˙t had sex
with Mrs Mills

1397
01:21:18,130 --> 01:21:20,320
in a very long while.

1398
01:21:22,210 --> 01:21:24,387
Is that meant to be clever, Sir John?

1399
01:21:24,470 --> 01:21:27,639
I didn˙t come here to be clever,
I came here to tell the truth.

1400
01:21:27,640 --> 01:21:31,405
We have heard evidence to
the contrary from members of the staff.

1401
01:21:31,550 --> 01:21:34,590
Then it˙s entirely mistaken.

1402
01:21:37,320 --> 01:21:40,690
Sir John, let us be
entirely clear about this.

1403
01:21:42,890 --> 01:21:44,890
Are you saying you have never been

1404
01:21:44,930 --> 01:21:47,450
in a compromising situation
with Mrs Mills

1405
01:21:47,900 --> 01:21:52,380
since you and she were lovers
some 16 years ago?

1406
01:21:53,070 --> 01:21:55,820
If you read back
the tribunal reporter˙s notes,

1407
01:21:56,270 --> 01:21:59,110
you will find exactly what I said.

1408
01:21:59,610 --> 01:22:04,030
Are you saying that you have never
had sex with her in all that while?

1409
01:22:04,710 --> 01:22:06,079
Is that what you˙re telling us?

1410
01:22:06,080 --> 01:22:09,270
I have already told you.
Do you think I˙m a liar?

1411
01:22:10,690 --> 01:22:14,470
Well, we think no such thing,
Sir John, we...

1412
01:22:16,790 --> 01:22:19,810
We could not. We could not.

1413
01:22:22,000 --> 01:22:24,369
Is there anything else
you wish to share with us,

1414
01:22:24,370 --> 01:22:26,253
before we consider our findings?

1415
01:22:26,370 --> 01:22:27,450
Yes.

1416
01:22:29,870 --> 01:22:32,650
Mrs Mills is a hard-working
Queens Counsel

1417
01:22:33,110 --> 01:22:35,130
who has helped a lot of people

1418
01:22:35,480 --> 01:22:38,880
who would not otherwise
have found access to justice.

1419
01:22:39,450 --> 01:22:42,520
This hearing is shabby and unjust

1420
01:22:43,050 --> 01:22:47,090
and I believe that it has another
and altogether sinister agenda.

1421
01:22:47,720 --> 01:22:50,759
It has been brought about for reasons
which I would suggest

1422
01:22:50,760 --> 01:22:55,120
are the opposite of those ideals
of fairness and decency

1423
01:22:56,630 --> 01:22:59,210
which you and I have sworn to uphold.

1424
01:23:02,410 --> 01:23:06,352
Well, you˙re entitled to express
your opinion, Sir John. We note it.

1425
01:23:08,780 --> 01:23:13,090
We shall retire for a moment
before we report.

1426
01:23:17,520 --> 01:23:19,040
(SIGHING)

1427
01:23:19,960 --> 01:23:21,889
What do you think this is all about?

1428
01:23:21,890 --> 01:23:24,230
I think this is all about to end now.

1429
01:23:24,630 --> 01:23:27,350
They may yet present their photos.

1430
01:23:27,800 --> 01:23:29,170
Well, we˙ll soon know.

1431
01:23:37,370 --> 01:23:40,194
Well, I˙m not going to call
for closing speeches.

1432
01:23:44,080 --> 01:23:45,963
Having considered the testimony,

1433
01:23:46,250 --> 01:23:49,560
and the particular weight
to what Sir John Deed told us,

1434
01:23:50,090 --> 01:23:54,480
that he did not
have sexual relations with Mrs Mills,

1435
01:23:55,160 --> 01:23:57,790
we can do no other
than to take his word.

1436
01:23:58,230 --> 01:24:00,510
Therefore the case is dismissed.

1437
01:24:11,270 --> 01:24:13,200
Congratulations, Jo.

1438
01:24:13,580 --> 01:24:15,279
They didn˙t find me not guilty, Simon.

1439
01:24:15,280 --> 01:24:17,279
They didn˙t believe me
or even exonerate me.

1440
01:24:17,280 --> 01:24:19,279
They were simply obliged
to believe John.

1441
01:24:19,280 --> 01:24:20,949
You˙re innocent, Jo, end of story.

1442
01:24:20,950 --> 01:24:23,170
But they don˙t believe it.

1443
01:24:23,550 --> 01:24:27,550
It˙s better than having the case proven
and being taken off the road.

1444
01:24:27,660 --> 01:24:29,896
Do you think I˙d ever let that happen?

1445
01:24:30,990 --> 01:24:34,579
I have no problem with losing
when it˙s an even playing field.

1446
01:24:34,760 --> 01:24:37,999
It never is with John. He seems to think
anyone who made a profit in business

1447
01:24:38,000 --> 01:24:39,139
did so by foul means.

1448
01:24:39,140 --> 01:24:41,493
Calm down, darling,
all is far from lost.

1449
01:24:41,870 --> 01:24:45,470
Why didn˙t you produce
the photographs of them in bed?

1450
01:24:46,040 --> 01:24:47,060
To have done so

1451
01:24:47,280 --> 01:24:51,339
in the face of His Lordship denying
they had an affair or were in bed,

1452
01:24:51,550 --> 01:24:54,021
would be to bring the bench
into disrepute.

1453
01:24:54,250 --> 01:24:57,689
To say nothing of having to admit
that your staff at the lodgings

1454
01:24:57,690 --> 01:24:59,800
broke into his bedroom.

1455
01:25:01,460 --> 01:25:05,329
The government has as much, if not more
to lose than your clients, George.

1456
01:25:05,330 --> 01:25:07,329
We˙re as anxious as you
to see this case founder,

1457
01:25:07,330 --> 01:25:10,154
assuming, as you say,
there is no case to answer.

1458
01:25:10,500 --> 01:25:13,690
That depends on whether he admits
the illegal evidence.

1459
01:25:14,200 --> 01:25:17,083
We˙ve been trying
to help you there, Mrs Channing.

1460
01:25:18,070 --> 01:25:20,679
Our research department
has found every precedent

1461
01:25:20,680 --> 01:25:23,400
for refusal to admit tainted evidence.

1462
01:25:25,350 --> 01:25:28,849
My Lord, I know you have heard arguments
but before you give your ruling

1463
01:25:28,850 --> 01:25:32,319
on whether or not to admit
the illegally discovered evidence

1464
01:25:32,320 --> 01:25:34,070
on behalf of the claimant,

1465
01:25:34,390 --> 01:25:36,508
I would like you to give full weight

1466
01:25:36,760 --> 01:25:39,920
to the principle
behind the Civil Procedure Rules

1467
01:25:40,430 --> 01:25:43,010
to deal with cases justly.

1468
01:25:44,100 --> 01:25:46,090
I would implore you to exclude

1469
01:25:46,440 --> 01:25:49,029
the unlawfully obtained emails
on this basis.

1470
01:25:49,340 --> 01:25:51,458
Or would you like to see the photos?

1471
01:25:52,910 --> 01:25:55,490
What photos, Mrs Channing?

1472
01:25:55,910 --> 01:25:59,630
Ah, the photocopies
of the authority, My Lord.

1473
01:26:01,450 --> 01:26:04,290
I think you˙re being facetious,
Mrs Channing.

1474
01:26:06,120 --> 01:26:08,059
However, I am denying the claimant

1475
01:26:08,060 --> 01:26:11,250
the right to use this
illegally discovered information.

1476
01:26:11,760 --> 01:26:14,629
My Lord, can I direct you
to Kuruma and the Crown?

1477
01:26:14,630 --> 01:26:17,290
No, Mrs Mills,
I don˙t need to hear any more.

1478
01:26:18,470 --> 01:26:21,470
Giving carte blanche
for the illegal trawl of emails

1479
01:26:21,540 --> 01:26:24,850
would set a bad precedent.
The evidence is tainted.

1480
01:26:25,410 --> 01:26:27,309
I can˙t allow it.
To do so would be unsafe.

1481
01:26:27,310 --> 01:26:29,860
Then I would argue
under Section 3, My Lord,

1482
01:26:30,280 --> 01:26:33,079
that as the main plank
of the claimant˙s case has fallen,

1483
01:26:33,080 --> 01:26:34,279
there is no claim to answer.

1484
01:26:34,280 --> 01:26:36,449
I would therefore ask you
to throw out the claim.

1485
01:26:36,450 --> 01:26:39,089
DEED: Yes, I can see
where you˙re coming from.

1486
01:26:39,090 --> 01:26:42,659
But before I give my ruling,
I need to know if the electronic search

1487
01:26:42,660 --> 01:26:45,729
I ordered on behalf of the claimant
has yielded any results

1488
01:26:45,730 --> 01:26:48,083
that might affect my decision.
Mrs Mills?

1489
01:26:48,230 --> 01:26:51,199
Our data recovery experts
did find other erased emails

1490
01:26:51,200 --> 01:26:54,510
that relate directly to the action.
Nine, in fact.

1491
01:26:55,040 --> 01:26:58,393
The most telling of these was one
sent on December 9, 2000

1492
01:26:58,410 --> 01:27:00,900
by Tim Listfield,
the CEO of One-Way PLC,

1493
01:27:01,310 --> 01:27:04,193
to Max Solveigh, the marketing director.
It reads,

1494
01:27:04,310 --> 01:27:07,849
"Max, what tosh. We don˙t spend
all these millions developing our phones

1495
01:27:07,850 --> 01:27:11,719
"to have a bunch of pinheads tell us
they could be harming customers.

1496
01:27:11,720 --> 01:27:13,940
"Find another result."

1497
01:27:14,320 --> 01:27:16,589
My Lord,
you can˙t admit this, you agreed.

1498
01:27:16,590 --> 01:27:20,329
No, Mrs Channing, I agreed not to
admit evidence gathered illegally.

1499
01:27:20,330 --> 01:27:23,699
I made an order for this discovery.
I˙m going to admit this evidence.

1500
01:27:23,700 --> 01:27:26,739
My Lord, this is not in the spirit
of the Civil Procedure Rules.

1501
01:27:26,740 --> 01:27:28,760
DEED: Mrs Channing, I have ruled.

1502
01:27:29,140 --> 01:27:33,209
Unless you have an argument that relates
to this legally discovered material,

1503
01:27:33,210 --> 01:27:35,079
I˙m going to allow this case
to go forward.

1504
01:27:35,080 --> 01:27:40,000
Further, I˙m going to reserve it
to myself to be heard here in...

1505
01:27:43,020 --> 01:27:44,510
three weeks, Mr Harrison?

1506
01:27:45,490 --> 01:27:48,480
Three weeks, My Lord, the 30th?

1507
01:27:48,960 --> 01:27:51,420
DEED: The 30th it is. Until then.

1508
01:28:03,440 --> 01:28:05,382
You really are pushing your luck.

1509
01:28:05,440 --> 01:28:08,088
I expected
the defendant˙s counsel to be here.

1510
01:28:12,120 --> 01:28:14,670
One-Way are going to fight this,

1511
01:28:15,080 --> 01:28:16,949
and fight dirty, I shouldn˙t wonder.

1512
01:28:16,950 --> 01:28:18,959
- You˙re going to need some help.
- Not from you, thank you.

1513
01:28:18,960 --> 01:28:22,078
No, there˙s a Sergeant Bridges
who might prove useful.

1514
01:28:23,090 --> 01:28:25,580
I˙ll get Row Colemore
to put you in touch.

1515
01:28:27,600 --> 01:28:29,790
Do you want to see a film tonight?

1516
01:28:30,170 --> 01:28:34,582
I˙ve just about got my reputation back.
I˙m not in a hurry to risk it again.

1517
01:28:34,740 --> 01:28:37,369
Is there a risk, Jo?
You˙re not before me now.

1518
01:28:37,370 --> 01:28:40,530
Anything to do with you is a risk, John.

1519
01:28:40,830 --> 01:28:47,530
